*PPD-Adobe: "4.3"
*%
*% Brother PT-P710BT CUPS PPD (unofficial, community-written)
*%
*% Not affiliated with or endorsed by Brother Industries, Ltd. "Brother"
*% and "P-touch" are trademarks of Brother Industries, Ltd. This PPD
*% drives the printer via the rastertoptp710bt filter and the ptp710bt
*% backend included in this project; see README.md for install/pairing
*% instructions and known limitations.
*%
*FormatVersion: "4.3"
*FileVersion: "1.0"
*LanguageVersion: English
*LanguageEncoding: ISO8859-1
*PCFileName: "BRPTP710.PPD"
*Manufacturer: "Brother"
*Product: "(PT-P710BT)"
*cupsVersion: 2.0
*cupsSNMPSupplies: False
*cupsLanguages: "en"
*ModelName: "Brother PT-P710BT"
*ShortNickName: "Brother PT-P710BT"
*NickName: "Brother PT-P710BT, Bluetooth Raster (unofficial)"
*PSVersion: "(3010.000) 0"
*LanguageLevel: "3"
*ColorDevice: False
*DefaultColorSpace: Gray
*FileSystem: False
*Throughput: "1"
*TTRasterizer: Type42
*cupsManualCopies: True
*cupsFilter2: "application/vnd.cups-raster application/vnd.brother-ptp710bt-raster 0 rastertoptp710bt"

*OpenUI *PageSize/Tape Width: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 10 AnySetup *PageSize
*DefaultPageSize: mm12
*PageSize mm3.5/3.5mm Tape: "<</PageSize[10 28]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize mm6/6mm Tape: "<</PageSize[17 57]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize mm9/9mm Tape: "<</PageSize[26 85]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize mm12/12mm Tape: "<</PageSize[34 113]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize mm18/18mm Tape: "<</PageSize[51 170]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize mm24/24mm Tape: "<</PageSize[68 227]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *PageSize

*OpenUI *PageRegion/Tape Width: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 10 AnySetup *PageRegion
*DefaultPageRegion: mm12
*PageRegion mm3.5/3.5mm Tape: "<</PageSize[10 28]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageRegion mm6/6mm Tape: "<</PageSize[17 57]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageRegion mm9/9mm Tape: "<</PageSize[26 85]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageRegion mm12/12mm Tape: "<</PageSize[34 113]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageRegion mm18/18mm Tape: "<</PageSize[51 170]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageRegion mm24/24mm Tape: "<</PageSize[68 227]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *PageRegion

*DefaultImageableArea: mm12
*ImageableArea mm3.5/3.5mm Tape: "0 0 10 28"
*ImageableArea mm6/6mm Tape: "0 0 17 57"
*ImageableArea mm9/9mm Tape: "0 0 26 85"
*ImageableArea mm12/12mm Tape: "0 0 34 113"
*ImageableArea mm18/18mm Tape: "0 0 51 170"
*ImageableArea mm24/24mm Tape: "0 0 68 227"

*DefaultPaperDimension: mm12
*PaperDimension mm3.5/3.5mm Tape: "10 28"
*PaperDimension mm6/6mm Tape: "17 57"
*PaperDimension mm9/9mm Tape: "26 85"
*PaperDimension mm12/12mm Tape: "34 113"
*PaperDimension mm18/18mm Tape: "51 170"
*PaperDimension mm24/24mm Tape: "68 227"

*% Continuous tape has no fixed length: the widths/heights above are only
*% convenient presets (~40mm default label length). For a different label
*% length, use macOS's "Paper Size > Manage Custom Sizes..." and set the
*% width to match your loaded tape (the filter picks the tape width from
*% the actual page width in the print job, not from this preset's name).
*MaxMediaWidth: "68"
*MinMediaWidth: "10"
*MaxMediaHeight: "5000"
*MinMediaHeight: "20"
*HWMargins: 0 0 0 0
*CustomPageSize True: "<</PageSize[5 -2 roll]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*ParamCustomPageSize Width: "1 points 10 68"
*ParamCustomPageSize Height: "2 points 20 5000"
*ParamCustomPageSize WidthOffset: "0 points 0 0"
*ParamCustomPageSize HeightOffset: "0 points 0 0"
*ParamCustomPageSize Orientation: "0 int 0 0"

*OpenUI *AutoCut/Cut Each Label: Boolean
*OrderDependency: 10 AnySetup *AutoCut
*DefaultAutoCut: True
*AutoCut True/Yes: ""
*AutoCut False/No: ""
*CloseUI: *AutoCut

*OpenUI *Resolution/Resolution: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 10 AnySetup *Resolution
*DefaultResolution: 180dpi
*Resolution 180dpi/180 DPI: "<</HWResolution[180 180]>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *Resolution

*OpenUI *ColorModel/Color Mode: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 10 AnySetup *ColorModel
*DefaultColorModel: Gray
*ColorModel Gray/Black and White: "<</cupsColorSpace 0/cupsBitsPerColor 1/cupsColorOrder 0/cupsCompression 0>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *ColorModel

*cupsBitsPerColor: 1
*cupsColorOrder: Chunky
*cupsColorSpace: Gray
*cupsCompression: 0
